F07 TS gate - session 31 (2026-11-15, local branch, HEAD 002b969 + uncommitted work)

Cause of the one remaining F07 gate failure (attach-intent-f07.test.ts:215
"rebuilding an index clears every conversation-scoped key for it"): the shown
ledger is ONE root aggregate (.data/attach-index/.shown.json). writeShown and
shownDelete did read-modify-write with no cross-process serialization, so a
concurrent writer (vitest worker / Next worker) re-saved a map it had read
BEFORE the delete, resurrecting deleted keys and silently dropping the other
writer-scope keys. The defect was pre-existing (attach-turn-budget ledger pins
had the same latent exposure); F07 v2 made it observable.

Mechanism fix (lib/server/attachindex/store.ts): cross-process mutex for the
ledger read-modify-write.
  - SHOWN_LOCK = <file>.lock directory; mkdir is atomic across processes.
  - owner token file inside the lock; only the owner releases (foreign locks are
    never deleted by a non-owner).
  - stale break only on proof: lock dir mtime older than SHOWN_LOCK_STALE_MS
    (2000 ms) while every real critical section is a couple of sync fs calls;
    wait bound SHOWN_LOCK_WAIT_MS = 500 ms.
  - the map is re-read INSIDE the lock, so each mutation rebases on the latest
    file (no lost updates from other writers).
  - readers stay lock-free: durableWrite = unique temp file + rename, so a
    reader sees the whole old map or the whole new map.
  - lock contention/wedge falls back to a rebase-without-mutex merge and never
    throws: the ledger stays an optimization, never a turn failure.
  - writeShown/shownDelete now mutate through withShownLock(); no file added
    inside any attachment dir, .shown.json stays a ROOT aggregate (store-fixture
    golden file-set contract preserved).

